bodyguard-of-bits (0.4.7-1) UNRELEASED; urgency=low

  * Maintenance release — documentation audit, UI cosmetic harmonization,
    bash completion overhaul, and CI release automation. No behavior
    change in the audit pipeline.
  * Cross-documentation audit: 24 corrections across 8 files (README,
    README_FR, README_TECH + FR, README_DEV + FR, SECURITY_FR,
    man/bob.1, man/bob-profile.5, AUTOMATION + FR). Stale claims
    rectified: "9 domains" -> 7, profile table corrected (the docker
    profile listed but never existed; workstation is an alias to
    desktop; container is the real third profile), --list-checks /
    --list-profiles / --min-level=info / --format=text doc-only flags
    removed (they don't exist in cli.py), webhook JSON sample
    structure corrected (alerts/warnings are integer counts not
    arrays of objects), webhook timeout 5s -> 10s, max profile
    extends depth 5 -> 8 levels.
  * New internal cartography: DOCUMENTS/SNAPSHOT.md (~640 lines)
    providing a single-doc bird's-eye view of the codebase for
    refactor preparation and sub-agent briefing. Internal doc,
    not shipped in bob-core.docs.
  * UI cosmetic: gauge bars in --watch, --breakdown, per-domain
    scores, and --manage-logs history now share a single coloured
    rendering via bob.output.score_bar() — green (score >= 8),
    yellow (5-7), red (0-4). Matches the existing disk partition
    bars in display._disk_bar. Affects display only; --no-color
    continues to neutralise the colours.
  * Bash completion (bob/data/bob.bash-completion) comprehensive
    overhaul. Critical fix: --check=, --skip=, --min-level=,
    --format=, --profile=, --lang=, --target=, --webhook-format=,
    --output= TAB-completions of values were all silently failing
    because the function read ${COMP_WORDS[COMP_CWORD]} which
    returns "=" when bash splits on the default COMP_WORDBREAKS.
    Fix: use the bash-completion positional-argument convention
    ($2 / $3) which provides the clean current word stripped of
    the '=' word-break prefix. Also: function renamed _ufw_audit
    -> _bob (legacy name from before the project rename); dead
    code removed (_ufw_audit_install for install.sh which no
    longer exists); section list factored and made to match
    `bob --check=list` exactly (was missing iptables_nft, samba,
    desktop_apps); long-options list now matches cli.py exactly
    (added --check=, --skip=, --output-dir=, --breakdown,
    --no-colour); short-options gained -B (--breakdown).
  * CI: .github/workflows/publish.yml gains a 4th job
    "github-release" that runs after PyPI publish succeeds. It
    extracts the release title from CHANGELOG.md table row, body
    from DOCUMENTS/CHANGELOG_FULL.md section, creates the GitHub
    release via softprops/action-gh-release@v2 with the wheel and
    sdist as attached assets, marks as latest. Removes the
    manual `gh release create` step.
  * 4500 tests (unchanged from v0.4.6). 3 tests in
    tests/test_breakdown.py::TestBar adapted to strip ANSI escape
    sequences before asserting visible bar content.

 -- Cédric Clauzel <cedricclauzel@mailo.com>  Thu, 21 May 2026 09:00:00 +0200

bodyguard-of-bits (0.4.6-1) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Terrain test pass v0.4.5 fixes (2 reproducible bugs across 13 audits
    on 6 distinct systems, including production hardware).
  * Bug 1: bob/checks/kernel_modules.py — dpkg-query did not filter on
    'ii' state, so kernels left in 'rc' state after `apt remove` (without
    --purge) were still listed as installed. Now uses
    ${db:Status-Abbrev}|${Package} and keeps only lines whose 2nd char
    is 'i' (covers 'ii' and 'hi'; excludes 'rc', 'pn', 'un', 'iU').
  * Bug 2: bob/domain_scores.py::active_domains_from_engine() — scoring
    inversion after remediation. The actionable filter widened from
    (WARN, ALERT) to (OK, WARN, ALERT), so a domain that goes clean
    (only `updates.ok` left) stays at 10/10 in the global average
    instead of disappearing from the denominator. INFO-only domains
    remain hidden by design.
  * 4500 tests (+11 vs v0.4.5).
  * Multi-distro integration CI (additive): GitHub Actions matrix runs
    BOB inside containers of Debian 12/13, Ubuntu 22.04/24.04/25.04,
    Kali Rolling, Fedora 41 on every push/PR to main.

 -- Cédric Clauzel <cedricclauzel@mailo.com>  Sun, 17 May 2026 17:45:45 +0200

bodyguard-of-bits (0.4.5-1) UNRELEASED; urgency=low

  * Test infrastructure hardening release (pure refactor of
    tests/test_locale_coverage.py — no source file in bob/ modified).
  * Switched the locale-coverage scanner from regex over Python source
    to ast.parse + ast.walk. Eliminates three classes of regex false
    positive: docstring matches, multi-line call site fragility, and
    obj._t(...) attribute calls. The _KEY_EXCLUSIONS allowlist that
    was the symptom of the regex limitation is deleted.
  * Same external contract: 9 tests in TestLocaleCoverage +
    TestExplainNamespaceCoverage + TestPlaceholderParity.
  * 4489 tests (unchanged total vs v0.4.4).

